    description: "FOUND 2026-08-25 while re-deriving INV-busis's escape-cause breakdown on the\np4_busis_08252026 corpus (pretix, caddy, alertmanager, kserve).\n\nTHE DEFECT, one line. scripts/measure-call-escape-cause.py:227 filters escape\nsites down to call nodes with a bare string equality against the PYTHON node\ntype:\n\n    if cache[sym].get(line) != \"call\":\n        continue\n\n_node_types() returns tree-sitter node types verbatim, and Go's call nodes are\ncall_expression and deferred_call, never \"call\". So for a Go repository the\nfilter discards every site and the instrument reports zero call-node escapes\nhowever many there are.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, both arms of the same corpus run, same tree, same\ninvocation:\n\n  caddy, cause arm    : \"=== CALL-node escape sites: 0 ===\"\n  caddy, shapes arm   : 97 blocked sites including call_expression 2 and\n                        deferred_call 2 (plus go_statement 3 in production)\n\nThe shapes arm is unaffected because it emits node_type as DATA and lets the\nconsumer classify, rather than hardcoding one language's spelling in a filter.\n\nWHY THE ZERO IS DANGEROUS RATHER THAN MERELY WRONG. The cause arm's positive\ncontrol FIRED on that same caddy run -- 78,600 edges offered, 9,737 callees_at\nentries, 236 escape events captured -- so the harness was demonstrably alive\nand only the call-node filter was blind. A zero under a live positive control\nis exactly the shape a reader trusts. Read literally it says \"Go produces no\ncall-node escape sites\", i.e. the INV-linub / INV-mumov causes do not affect\nGo, which is a claim about a LANGUAGE drawn from an instrument that never\nlooked at that language.\n\nBLAST RADIUS IN THE CURRENT RUN: caddy and alertmanager (both Go) are affected;\npretix and kserve (both Python) are not. alertmanager's cause arm was still\nrunning when this was found and will carry the same false zero.\n\nFIX: replace the equality with a membership test over a named set of call node\ntypes, with each member justified in a comment -- including an explicit ruling\non whether go_statement / deferred_call count as call SITES or as wrappers\naround one, since the shapes arm currently reports them separately and the two\ninstruments must agree or their numbers cannot be reconciled. Then re-run the\ncause arm for the Go repos only; the Python arms need no re-run.\n\nNOT FIXED IMMEDIATELY AND THIS IS DELIBERATE: run-corpus.sh invokes the script\nas a fresh subprocess per arm, so editing it mid-run would leave the arms\ndiffering in more than one hunk (LIVE.md rule 14). Fix after the run exits."  # 5799
    fields: {}  # 5799
- op: discuss  # aa1c
