  message: "CORRECTION TO THE FILING, same day, and it WIDENS the item.\n\nThe filing says the defect affects \"caddy and alertmanager (both Go); pretix\nand kserve (both Python) are not\". That rested on an assumption I did not\ncheck: one language per repository. It is false for this corpus. Measured by\nfile extension over production blocked-escape sites:\n\n    pretix        python 15   javascript 5\n    kserve        python 34   go 14\n    caddy         go 91\n    alertmanager  go 4\n    POOLED        go 109   python 49   javascript 5\n\nkserve carries 14 GO sites and pretix carries 5 JAVASCRIPT ones. The\n`!= \"call\"` filter drops those silently too, so EVERY repo in the corpus is\naffected, not two -- and the affected share is invisible in a repo that also\ncontains Python, because the Python sites still come through and the arm looks\nlike it worked.\n\nCONSEQUENCE: the cause arm must be re-run for ALL FOUR repos after the fix, not\nfor the Go pair. The prior claim that the Python arms \"need no re-run\" is\nwithdrawn.\n\nTHIS ALSO SHARPENS THE FIX. Adding Go's spellings to the comparison would\nrepeat the original mistake one language later, and a mixed-language repo is\nexactly the case where the resulting silence is least visible. The fix should\nbe a per-language map plus a LOUD REFUSAL when a language present in the data\nhas no entry -- the same fail-closed-and-say-so shape analyzer_disclosure.py\nuses for method-call emission, and the same shape\nmeasure-escape-closing-ceiling.py already uses when its own monkeypatch does\nnot take (\"the run says so and refuses the corpus table rather than printing\nzeros that look like findings\")."  # aa1c
